@startuml remote-worker-retire
!theme plain
title Retire a remote worker: both sides can end it alone; the identity stays pinned unless revoked

actor "Operator (our side)" as OP
participant "Registry / key keeper" as T
participant "Dispatcher + helper\n(our host)" as D
participant "Bridge" as BR
actor "Donor (the machine's owner)" as ADM
participant "curator remote-worker\n(donor)" as C
participant "Privileged helper (donor)" as PH

== our side ==
OP -> T: revoke grants; optionally revoke K (root-signed record)
OP -> D: drop workplace
D -> D: stop processes; remove authorized_keys; archive home; delete user; remove firewall rules
BR -> BR: next frame from K refused (revoked / no workplace); mailbox closed
note right of BR: the donor's connection drops; its supervisor stops the harness\nand reports "retired by project"

== donor side ==
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker stop
C -> C: end the harness user's processes; mark stopped; audit line
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker revoke
C -> C: delete keyring item (K), locked config, managed home, audit kept for the donor
C -> PH: remove user, firewall rules, sandbox profile, units
PH --> C: done
C --> ADM: removed; nothing of the project remains on this machine

note over OP, PH
  Return: the same identity K may be given a new workplace later (new package, new init --rejoin)
  unless K was revoked; a revoked K must re-join with a new key.
end note
@enduml
